# Omid Edge Panel — Graphical UI Refresh (2026-10-16)

- Updated the root landing page to the latest gaming-inspired platform design.
- Updated the Persian login page and both configuration-error pages with the shared neon/HUD visual system.
- Updated the admin dashboard UI using the supplied full dashboard HTML.
- Synchronized the HTML assets with the bundled pages embedded in `_worker.js` for standalone Worker deployments.
- Backend routing and API handler logic were left unchanged by this UI refresh.

# Omid Edge Panel — Platform Ecosystem Landing Page (2026-10-16)

- Rebuilt the root landing page with a platform-first layout and a single primary panel-entry button.
- Added distinct sections for Cloudflare Workers, Cloudflare Pages, GitHub, GitHub Actions, Telegram, and YouTube.
- Preserved existing Worker routes and backend behavior while updating only the landing-page HTML.

# Omid Edge Panel — Login Session Compatibility Fix (2026-10-16)

- Made the `auth` cookie derivation consistent across login and admin requests; it no longer depends on the User-Agent string.
- This fixes a possible login-success / redirect-back-to-login loop when the User-Agent differs between requests.

# Omid Edge Panel — Standalone Worker UI Fix (2026-10-16)

- Changed the standalone Worker frontend fallback from the original upstream Pages site to the branded `omidiran35-bwv.pages.dev` deployment.
- Ignores a stale `PAGES_URL` value that points directly to `edt-pages.github.io`, while retaining support for an explicitly configured custom Pages frontend.

- Added a branded neon OMID-IRAN favicon to the landing page, admin dashboard, login, and configuration pages.
- Network information cards now resolve flags from full country names as well as ISO country codes.
# Omid Edge Panel — Config naming update (2026-10-15)

- Branded generated ordinary links as `🟢 OMID-IRAN | ALL NN`, ECH links as `🔵 OMID-IRAN | MCI-TCI NN`, and FinalMask + Cipher Suites links as `🟡 OMID-IRAN | MTN-RTL NN`. Each group has its own two-digit sequence.
- FinalMask + Cipher Suites links use the `fp=unsafe` fingerprint.

