## [2.1.20260904162413] - 2026-09-04 16:24:13

### ADD

- Added ALPN field support; node links now include the ALPN parameter automatically for broader client compatibility.

### Debug

- Fixed HTTPS proxy handshakes when an upstream requests a client certificate (`CertificateRequest`); an empty certificate is now returned to complete the handshake. [Commit](https://github.com/cmliu/CF-Workers-CheckSocks5/commit/ae93bc28462a6df03795143a5caa85f717ba231a)

## [2.1.20260811144522] - 2026-08-11 14:45:22

### Change

- Optimized XHTTP uploads by batching small chunks before sending, reducing frequent writes and resource overhead and improving large-file uploads.

## [2.1.20260810030901] - 2026-08-10 03:09:01

### ADD

- Added receiver support for XHTTP obfuscation padding headers using `xPaddingObfsMode` (tokenish / queryInHeader).

## [2.1.20260809231057] - 2026-08-09 23:10:57

### Debug

- Fixed XHTTP chained-proxy parsing to accept trailing slashes in paths.

## [2.1.20260809201158] - 2026-08-09 20:11:58

### Change

- Optimized the XHTTP data path: TCP data now flows directly in both directions through `request.body.pipeTo(socket.writable)` and `socket.readable.pipeTo(IdentityTransformStream)`, bypassing intermediate stream queues and per-chunk BYOB/Grain handling to reduce CPU usage.
- Improved XHTTP connection management: `forwardataTCP` can now establish a connection and write the first packet before returning the socket for direct piping, while retaining the reverse-proxy fallback if direct dialing fails. gRPC and WebSocket callers are unaffected.
- Refactored XHTTP UDP handling into a dedicated branch while preserving Trojan UDP reverse-proxy and DNS-forwarding behavior.

## [2.1.20260729235734] - 2026-07-29 23:57:34

### Change

- Corrected `PRELOAD_RACE_DIAL`: the default is now `false`; set `1` or `true` to enable preloaded race dialing. Updated the README accordingly. [Commit](https://github.com/cmliu/edgetunnel/commit/aea8b85688ef6066116af551cfd5e6fd2ce77567)

## [2.1.20260724150359] - 2026-07-24 15:03:59

### Change

- Synced the latest GrainTCP transport improvements: increased the upload batching target from `16KB` to `20KB` and reused the shared batching core to reduce frequent `writer.write()` calls. [Upstream commit](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Optimized downstream GrainTCP batching with a `32KB` cap, low-watermark checks, and timely flushes to reduce small WebSocket frames. [Upstream commit](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Optimized downstream packet handling to send large chunks directly and copy aggregated results before sending, preventing reusable-buffer corruption. [Upstream commit](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Enhanced TCP connection management using connection generations, socket identity, and drain barriers to keep asynchronous cleanup from affecting replacement connections. [Upstream reference](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Unified direct, segmented, and timed-flush sends into a serial send chain and preserved async send errors; response headers are consumed only on the first real send. [Upstream reference](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Preserved multi-protocol compatibility and bounded the local upload queue at `16MiB / 4096` entries to prevent unbounded queue growth. [Upstream change](https://github.com/ToiCF/GrainTCP/commit/1d22628f4d1413989f521f1d41591b0c72e658eb)
- Local speed-test responses now apply only in reverse-proxy mode; SOCKS5/HTTP/HTTPS/TURN/SSTP proxies forward speed-test requests normally.

## [2.1.20260722191426] - 2026-07-22 19:14:26

### Change

- Added support for the real connection test URL `http://cp.cloudflare.com/generate_204`.

## [2.1.20260711190235] - 2026-07-11 19:02:35

### ADD

- Added the `TCP_CONCURRENT_DIAL` environment variable to customize concurrent TCP dials; when set, the value is no longer reduced automatically for China Mobile.
- Added the `PROXY_CONCURRENT_DIAL` environment variable to customize concurrent proxy dials.

## [2.1.20260711022318] - 2026-07-11 02:23:18

### Change

- Improved reverse-proxy handling to prevent parameters for multiple proxy nodes from being overwritten by global variables.
- Improved DoH caching by temporarily caching recent positive and negative DNS lookups to reduce repeat requests and resource use.

### ADD

- Added configurable concurrent proxy dials. Higher values may improve connection speed but can switch IPs more often; lower values may improve stability.
- Added subscription-conversion options for UDP, XUDP, TLS 1.3, appending node type, and basic node sorting, and forwards them to the conversion backend.
- Added Trojan fallback proxy support. A backup proxy can be configured and used automatically when the primary connection fails.[PR #1359](https://github.com/cmliu/edgetunnel/pull/1359)

